    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs6Qjo2n",
      "title": "fix: add Ethereum address checksum validation tool",
      "author": "crStiv",
      "number": 953,
      "body": "## Implemented Features:\r\n- New Go tool in `ops/cmd/check_addresses` that finds and fixes incorrectly checksummed Ethereum addresses\r\n- Added CI check to prevent merging files with incorrect address formats\r\n- Tool can check specific files, all TOML files, or just the standard-versions-sepolia.toml\r\n- Fails with exit code 1 when bad addresses are found (for CI integration)\r\n\r\n## Background:\r\nIssue #938 pointed out that non-checksummed addresses cause problems when importing into Solidity. So I guess my fix can help with solving the issue.\r\n\r\n## Testing Done:\r\nI've tested this by manually invalidating addresses and confirming the tool catches and fixes them correctly. Added docs explaining usage and command flags.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots:\r\n1. Start of the process\r\n![Screenshot 2025-03-28 135243](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/00e1058d-ef80-4215-8467-fdfa57f57fee)\r\n2. The tool finding an incorrect address\r\n![Screenshot 2025-03-28 135301](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70013729-ba2f-4cc2-b133-20f87ce0124d)\r\n3. Fixing it with the `-fix` flag\r\n![Screenshot 2025-03-28 135411](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/71c35fe4-0aa6-4e72-8ed0-394131ebf609)\r\n4. Verifying all addresses now pass validation\r\n![Screenshot 2025-03-28 135533](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/655851aa-2d67-4c2a-bdeb-06c95f77789c)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2025-03-28T13:07:27Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 376,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs6IFggX",
      "title": "add river chain",
      "author": "jake-nyquist",
      "number": 834,
      "body": "<!--\r\nThis default template is a guide for PRs adding new chains to the registry.\r\nFor other types of PRs, please delete this template and write a brief description of your \r\ncode changes and rationale.\r\n -->\r\n\r\n# Adding a New Chain\r\nThis PR adds River Mainnet to the registry.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n- [x] I have declared the chain at the appropriate [Superchain Level](../docs/glossary.md#superchain-level-and-rollup-stage).\r\n- [x] I have run `just validate <chain-id>` locally to ensure all local validation checks pass. \r\n- [x] I have run `just codegen` to ensure that the chainlist and other generated files are up-to-date and include my chain.\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2025-01-17T01:11:44Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 251,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs70KzuM",
      "title": "ops: Support super-root game types",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 1290,
      "body": "Classify respected `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` type 5 as permissioned and `SUPER_CANNON_KONA` type 9 as permissionless during codegen. Temporarily pin the optimism dependency to the head of ethereum-optimism/optimism#21928.\n\nKeep this draft until ethereum-optimism/optimism#21928 merges, then repin to the resulting `develop` commit. The PR-head module currently requires a prepared checkout because its generated, gitignored `op-core/superchain/superchain-configs.zip` is absent from a clean module download; that must also be resolved before marking this ready.\n\nTests: `go test ./internal/manage -count=1` with a temporary `go.work` replacement to the prepared optimism PR checkout.\n\nCloses https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/issues/21711",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-21T04:07:51Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-07-28T08:54:24Z",
      "additions": 83,
      "deletions": 44
    },
